  "notes": "Validator class changes the color of form elements to error or success based on input's validation rules.\n\nNeeds daisyUI installed (npm i -D daisyui, then @plugin \"daisyui\" in your CSS).\n\nOriginal file: https://github.com/saadeghi/daisyui/blob/master/packages/docs/src/routes/(routes)/components/validator/+page.md",
  "code": "<form class=\"fieldset bg-base-200 border-base-300 rounded-box w-xs border p-4\">\n  <fieldset class=\"fieldset\">\n    <label class=\"label\">Email</label>\n    <input type=\"email\" class=\"input validator\" placeholder=\"Email\" required />\n    <p class=\"validator-hint hidden\">Required</p>\n  </fieldset>\n\n  <label class=\"fieldset\">\n    <span class=\"label\">Password</span>\n    <input type=\"password\" class=\"input validator\" placeholder=\"Password\" required />\n    <span class=\"validator-hint hidden\">Required</span>\n  </label>\n\n  <button class=\"btn btn-neutral mt-4\" type=\"submit\">Login</button>\n  <button class=\"btn btn-ghost mt-1\" type=\"reset\">Reset</button>\n</form>",
